# Issue: the scheduler's method-use maps (AUses), the allocator's walk of them
# (RSchedule) and AState's enable/mux port lists were in Ord Id (intern) order.
# Fix: AUses numbers each use where its elaboration-order walk first meets
# it and every later pass keeps that order.
# Pull request: https://github.com/MatX-inc/bsc/pull/198
# Probe: each module's Verilog alone versus behind two scramblers that intern
# its names the other way; before the fix EnableOrder's enable terms and mux
# arms swap and ArbOrder's arbiter (-resource-simple) conflicts another pair.

batching_verilog_pair EnableOrder.bsv mkEnableOrder EnableOrderTop.bsv mkEnableOrderTop {EnableOrderScrambleA.bsv EnableOrderScrambleB.bsv}

batching_verilog_pair ArbOrder.bsv mkArbOrder ArbOrderTop.bsv mkArbOrderTop {ArbOrderScrambleA.bsv ArbOrderScrambleB.bsv} {-resource-simple}
